    "description": "The tilde ``~`` operator returns the opposite value, bit by bit. The value is first converted to an integer, then, negated. This operator returns an integer.\n\n``~`` is often confused with ``!``, as some usages quite overlap.\n",
    "code": "<?php\n\n    $a = 3;     // 3 \n    $b = ~$a;   // -4\n    $c = !$a;   // false\n\n?>",
